  "name": "Science and Technology Committee (Commons)",
  "parent_committee_id": null,
  "purpose": "<p>The Science and Technology Committee is appointed by the House of Commons to examine the expenditure, administration and policy of the Government Office for Science and associated public bodies. It also examines science and technology policy across government and aims to ensure that policies and decision-making across departments are based on solid scientific evidence and advice.</p>\r\n<p>Follow us on social media:&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/hoccommittees.parliament.uk\">Bluesky</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61579513151155\">Facebook</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ukcommonscommittees\">Instagram</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/house-of-commons-committees\">LinkedIn</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/user/UKCommonsCommittees/\">Reddit</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://x.com/HoCcommitteesUK\">X</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLj3mInRJqIekxA--aDW780T_TUCwjea4M\">YouTube</a></u></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/email/committeecorridor\">Sign up to the&nbsp;weekly cross-committee newsletter, ‘Committee Corridor’.</a></p>",
